    "updated_at": "2023-06-03T14:46:14Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure how to apply that consistently. Many of these are statements describing the error state in exactly that fashion, e.g.,\r\n\r\n> An [IPv4 address](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-ipv4) ends with a U+002E (.).\r\n\r\nAlthough, maybe we should remove \"instead of U+002F (/)\" or put that between parenthesis? Nothing else has advice like that so maybe removing it would be best and make it clearer overall.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?",
